# EXTRACTION GUIDANCE & PATTERNS

> RGV loop (single source of truth), field inventory pattern, XML extraction patterns, few-shot examples.
> For detailed XML element patterns, see `lib/docs/xml-patterns-reference.md`.

---

## 1. RGV LOOP PATTERN (SINGLE SOURCE — DRY)

This is the core execution pattern for the entire agent. Phases 1-4 in `@00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` all reference this section — the pattern is defined here ONCE.

### The 6-Step RGV Loop

```
FOR EACH section to generate:
  STEP 1: RE-READ  — Fresh Read tool call on ALL relevant XML files for this section
  STEP 2: INVENTORY — Count target elements in XML, list names, COMMIT to count N
  STEP 3: GENERATE — Produce section content (must contain exactly N items)
  STEP 4: VERIFY  — Count generated items, compare to N
  STEP 5: FIX     — If mismatch → RE-READ XML, find missing, fix BEFORE proceeding
  STEP 6: CHECKPOINT — Emit micro-checkpoint with counts, write to file, proceed
```

### Why Each Step Matters

| Step | What It Prevents |
|------|------------------|
| RE-READ | Stale context — Phase 0 reads are for classification only |
| INVENTORY | Generates without knowing the target count → summarization |
| GENERATE | — |
| VERIFY | Undetected missing rows — the root cause of summarized tables |
| FIX | Errors propagating to the next section |
| CHECKPOINT | No audit trail of what was documented |

### VERIFY Is Not Optional

**VERIFY is the step that prevents summarization.** Without it, the agent can generate 20 of 161 mappings and move on, unaware rows are missing. With VERIFY, the agent compares 20 ≠ 161, stops, re-reads, and fixes.

