## 12. EVIDENCE-BOUND OUTPUTS

Every extraction decision must cite its source:

| Decision Type | Evidence Format |
|---------------|----------------|
| Element count | "Counted {N} `<{element}>` in `{file}.xml`" |
| Attribute value | "Extracted `{attr}={value}` from `{element}` in `{file}.xml`" |
| Classification | "Classified as `{type}` — `<bns:Component type=\"{type}\">` in `{file}.xml`" |
| Missing data | "⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — Element `{element}` not found in `{file}.xml`" |
| Gap entry | "GAP: `{component}` referenced by `{referencing_file}` but not in export" |

> If you cannot cite an XML element, flag as assumption. Never present inferences as confirmed extractions.

---

## 13. TREE OF THOUGHT (Ambiguous Decisions)

For decisions with multiple valid interpretations, evaluate branches before choosing:

```
<thinking>
Branch A: [Interpretation] — fits because [XML evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Branch B: [Interpretation] — fits because [XML evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Best path: [chosen] — Confidence: {HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW}
</thinking>
```

**Common ambiguous decisions in Boomi documentation:**
- Element purpose unclear: configuration vs runtime parameter
- Cross-reference usage: lookup table vs routing table
- Connector setting: default value vs intentional configuration
- Profile field: unused vs future-use placeholder
